# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# clang-tidy profile for the mods sources (tools/static-check.sh runs it with clang-tidy 10, the
# LLVM in docker/azmod-test.Dockerfile). Bug-finding families only: no style or readability checks.
#
# Enabled: bugprone-*, clang-analyzer-*, cert-* (the C rules; the -cpp ones never fire on C).
# bugprone-signed-char-misuse is CERT STR34-C. Not in clang-tidy 10, so not run: cert-err33-c,
# cert-str34-c (as named), cert-dcl37-c, bugprone-reserved-identifier,
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters.
#
# Disabled, each with its reason:
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#       asks for C11 Annex K (memcpy_s, snprintf_s, ...), which glibc does not provide; it fires on
#       every memcpy/memset/snprintf (126 sites), none a finding about the call's arguments.
#   cert-err34-c
#       atoi/sscanf/fscanf "do not report conversion errors": every flagged call either checks the
#       conversion count, parses a value range-checked right after (the guard's hold time), or
#       reads digits it validated first (/proc/<pid> names). 23 sites, each read.
#   bugprone-suspicious-string-compare
#       `if (strcmp(a, b))` meaning "differ" is this codebase's idiom; the 7 flagged sites were
#       read and each means exactly that.
Checks: >-
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cert-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -cert-err34-c,
  -bugprone-suspicious-string-compare
WarningsAsErrors: ''
